<Chapter id="why" label="So why did they win?" />

## So why did they win?

The Morning Ledger has already found the secret of success:

<WinnerStory />

It sounds almost reasonable. That is how the trick works.

The result came first. The explanation came second. Color, corners and edges never touched
the game.

Run it again. Maybe a new winner. Maybe the same one twice. The paper never prints
“chance.” It simply finds another reason.

Remember the headline we started with? How many reasons did you add before seeing the
mechanism?

<Chapter id="line-them-up" label="Line them up" />

## Line them up

A hundred circles, all different sizes, scattered around the room. I can spot the winner.
I cannot read the room.

So I cheat. First sort them. Then cut the wealth ruler into equal bins and drop one circle
into the matching pile. Move the number of piles and watch the picture change. The fortunes
do not.

<!--
  WIDGET: DistributionStage (R5, owner review 2026-07-08: "one stage for both sorting and
  log scale") — BinsStage + AxisStage merged into one stepper: room → sorted → binned →
  multiplying ruler. Built FROM the same circles the reader watched trade (latest logged
  run; the seeded reveal room as fallback). Bin width is a reader-visible choice, not
  nature's. Original circle coloring; no shape vocabulary needed here.
-->
<Deferred
  load={() => import('$lib/widgets/distribution/DistributionStage.svelte')}
  label="distribution stage"
  reserve="34rem"
/>

Now it is a histogram: the bars are the people you just watched. The cuts between bars are
my choice, not nature's. That is why the slider matters.

But the richest circle also owns the ruler. Fit it on a straight, adding scale and much of
the room is squeezed against zero. So change the ruler. Each step now *multiplies* by ten.
Equal distance means ten times the money; the hidden crowd opens up.

Below one cent goes in the dust box. Exact zero belongs there too: zero has no position on
a multiplying ruler. The new ruler reveals what the old one hid. It does not explain why
the shape exists.

